id: pm-context-ci-v2
title: Split quick PR CI from exhaustive local deep validation
description: "Fleet CI v2; companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required checks and committed dist verification, reduce deterministic seed depth for PRs, retain exhaustive npm/Bun gates after merge and nightly."
type: Task
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-context#234",performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T11:43:07.824Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T12:02:44.082Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Required test (22) and test (26) checks remain; docs-only fast path; full original gates retained in deep tier; unchanged coverage thresholds; evidence and timing recorded
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T11:43:10.343Z",codex-sol,"Search found no matching flaky or CI performance task. Existing pm-context-3zzd owns release changelog drift and remains separate. Required contexts are exactly test (22) and test (26); CodeQL is not required. Pilot PR is unbraind/pm-csv#258. Plan: hosted quick PR matrix, exhaustive local deep matrix, deterministic seed prefixes, unchanged coverage gates, bounded validation and early PR feedback. Companion: pm-cli-website-dyhg."
  "2026-11-15T11:45:13.803Z",codex-sol,"Detailed baseline log: run 43629665845 Node 22 execution 15m51s, Node 26 8m05s, queue-inclusive run 56m02s. Slowest seed corpora: answer reduction 113.59s, shared evidence 111.74s, task phase 80.55s, phase restoration 73.63s. Run 43623071562 --log-failed was empty; individual job log confirms npm release gate passed and changelog:check failed. No timed test failure was reported there. Removed unrelated since-packing one-second assertion in favor of its existing whole-pack serialization count and exact bytes. Release verifier files remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T11:47:01.796Z",codex-sol,"Implementation ready for early CI: ten seeded 500-case loops now use the deterministic 50-case quick prefix. Strict coverage thresholds and source scope unchanged. Added helper regression tests and scaled operational deadlines in affected process/lock tests; product serialization count replaces the fragile one-second assertion. Typecheck, test compilation, docstring lint and release-workflow verifier passed; strict unique-key YAML parse passed (actionlint unavailable). Local touched-test validation is running; the first linked invocation has the CLI default timeout and its metadata is corrected to 1200 seconds for subsequent execution."
  "2026-11-15T11:49:29.227Z",codex-sol,"PR opened as unbraind/pm-context#234 at head cee6a60559c4f8d12801e9c16cb282880f5497f9. Initial CI run 43710656373 and CodeQL run 43710656361 queued. Static workflow assertions and eight actual Bash classification fixtures passed, including nested executable tracker code, newline filenames and source-to-docs moves. The initial local pm test invocation hit its default 120-second watchdog without an assertion failure; rerunning with an explicit 1200-second timeout. Strict tracker health passes with pre-existing advisory warnings."
  "2026-11-15T11:53:38.482Z",codex-sol,"Touched quick suites passed 75/75 in 245.829 seconds with no failures, cancellations or skips. Separate scaled helper/receipt-lock run passed 5/5 in 7.349 seconds at PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3; bunx --no-install tsc --noEmit also passed. Running the single bounded quick coverage pass next. The default-timeout interruption was infrastructure configuration, not an assertion failure."
  "2026-11-15T12:02:43.229Z",codex-sol,"Single bounded quick coverage passed in 491.159 seconds: 489/489 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Native coverage 100% lines/branches/functions; c8 100% statements/lines/functions/branches, covering 6161 lines/statements, 269 functions and 2956 branches. Source scope and thresholds unchanged; no late-seed-only branch regressions required. Fresh build leaves committed dist unchanged. Baseline hosted Node 22 full npm gate was 7m46s, Bun 7m36s; different hardware and scope prevent a controlled speedup claim. Full depth intentionally reserved for CI Deep after merge. Initial hosted PR jobs remain queued after about 14 minutes, so completed job wall times are unavailable. Final evidence push will supersede that run. No review threads touched and no merges, item closes, protection or variable changes performed."
